  description="How to use Sopsdeck: install, edit secrets, grant Access, and keep encrypted files in Git."
  active="docs"
  narrow
>
  <section class="hero hero--compact">
    <p class="kicker">Documentation</p>
    <h1>Using Sopsdeck</h1>
    <p>
      Sopsdeck is under development. Expect issues, and
      <a href="https://github.com/sopsdeck/sopsdeck/issues/new">submit a GitHub issue</a> when you hit
      one.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="prose">
    <ul class="doc-index">
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/guide.html">Guide</a> — install, edit secrets, lock files, Access, and field encryption.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/guide.html#get-started">Get started</a> — <code>npx sopsdeck .</code> and your
        Age identity.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/guide.html#access">Access</a> — grant keys, request Access, and Project owners.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/changelog.html">Changelog</a> — generated from <code>CHANGELOG.md</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/glossary.html">Domain language</a> — Project, Managed File, Recipient, Access.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/versioning.html">Versioning</a> — Epoch SemVer; CHANGELOG.md is canonical.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/assets.html">Product assets</a> — stills, clips, walkthrough, and CLI casts.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/features.html">What tests prove</a> — living names generated from test titles.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/seams.html">Public seams</a> — where tests must live for contributors.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
